Non fictional text, especially of a scholarly subject, would seem likely to
have indirect questions.  Most Lojban text is fiction, and narrative fiction
seems less likely to have such constructions.  It is plausible that narrative
fiction that descrines mental states would have indirect clauses ("she
considered what to do next"), but I don't think much of that is included in
the Lojban text so far.

